The above output asserts different variables that were declared to track changes in `arraylist.` 

For example, Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount, New_arrListCount - 1) is used to ensure that by adding an element, the count of the arraylist is decremented by 1. 

Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListx, New_arrListx) confirms that the added element remains same.
 
Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrList_IndexOf_x, New_arrList_IndexOf_x) is used to verify that the new added index is present at the same index as before.

Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrList_LastIndexOf_x, New_arrList_LastIndexOf_x) validates whether a new element is added at last index or not.

Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrList_contains_x, New_arrList_contains_x) ensures that the added element is actually included in the list now.
 
